# Electron 44 has no npm install lifecycle script. Its module entrypoint
# downloads lazily on require() and does not honour ELECTRON_SKIP_BINARY_DOWNLOAD.
# Arena launches through an explicit no-download preflight instead:
#   npm run desktop:doctor
#   npm run desktop:prepare-electron  (explicit authorised binary download)
# Restricted dependency-only installs may use npm ci --ignore-scripts, but
# native dependencies then require separate supported preparation/verification.
#
# Dependency install-script decisions live in package.json "allowScripts"
# (npm >= 11.16 / 12 reads it from there; older npm ignores it entirely).
# No allow-scripts setting is set here on purpose: npm 12 warns that an
# .npmrc allow-scripts setting is ignored when package.json declares its
# own allowScripts field.
